+"""ops/notarize_ledgers.py — the ledger notary: what it writes, what it refuses, and how a notarized day is verified (E10 = LED-06,
+FX-EXEC 2026-09-13).
+
+*** SANDBOX ONLY: temp ledger trees, a temp git repo with a local bare remote, a fake `git` for failure injection, alarms with
+    LIVE_ALARM_SUPPRESS=1 into a temp audit file. Nothing live is read or written except the committed fixture below. ***
+
+★★★ THE MEASUREMENTS THAT PRODUCED THIS SUITE (2026-09-13, read-only on ~/dl_quant_live/state and the research repo)
+  (a) APPENDS READ AS TAMPERING. The notary recorded one whole-file sha256 per ledger file and its docstring promised "altering
+      any historical ledger breaks the chain". The ledger is append-only BY DESIGN: the markout backfill, ops/backfill_fills.py and
+      the 09-09 repair append rows to past days. Census of the live tree against all 43 manifests: 301 files, 259 unchanged,
+      42 grown — every one a pure append at a line boundary, zero bytes changed inside what was notarized. Under the whole-file
+      contract 42 of 43 days read "altered", so the notary could not tell a markout row from a forged fill.
+  (b) THE CHAIN BROKE, SILENTLY, 13 TIMES. Under launchd, `glob` on the research repo returned [] (it swallows the listing error)
+      and the manifest was written with prev = GENESIS; `git add` then died with "fatal: Unable to read current working directory:
+      Operation not permitted", a traceback nobody reads. Manifests 08-31..09-12 all carry GENESIS and none is committed. The same
+      observable is reproduced here with a directory of mode 0300 (create allowed, listing refused).
+  (c) HARDCODED BRANCH. The commit went to whatever branch was checked out and the push named `origin multi-asset-v2`; the research
+      repo is on another branch, so a commit that succeeded would never have reached the pushed branch — and the push's return code
+      was ignored while "committed+pushed" was printed.
+  (d) EVERY FILE IN THE DAY DIRECTORY was notarized (glob "*"), and `git add ledger_notary` + a pathspec-less `git commit` swept any
+      unrelated staged research file into a "notary:" commit.
+
+Each writer cell runs the tool as a subprocess: the new code with sandbox paths as arguments; the OLD code as a byte copy with only
+its two path constants rewritten to the sandbox (the logic under test is untouched, and the harness refuses if the rewrite does not
+match exactly once). Verifier cells call `verify_tree`; on the old module, which has no verifier, they read what the old module does
+offer — its whole-file-sha contract, through its own `sha()` — so an old-code failure is an assertion about that contract, not an
+AttributeError.
+"""
+import gzip
+import hashlib
+import json
+import os
+import shutil
+import subprocess
+import sys
+import tempfile
+import time
+
+HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
