+    since 08-06. A per-anchor gate reported PASS for a monitor that had watched nothing.
+  · The instrument that does measure the traded book already runs on THIS box: #55 `ops/ic_monitor.py` (launchd 01:30Z daily) judges
+    the rolling rank-IC of venue positions vs next-anchor returns and, since W1 (ef60f85, committed 2026-09-13T12:04:14Z), appends one
+    row per evaluation to `state/live/ic_monitor_evals.jsonl` (level / judged / r24 / r48 / trigger / judged_windows /
+    incomplete_windows / census{frontier_ts, newest_row_anchor_ts, r24, r48} / contract / eval_at). The live ledger did not exist yet
+    when this was written; its first row is due 2026-09-14T01:30Z.
+
+★★ WHAT THIS IS — AND IS NOT (§5-3). It checks the INPUT of a position-rank diagnostic: that #55 evaluated recently, that its row has
+   the contract shape, and that "not judged" comes with the census that explains it. It is NOT a model-score IC, NOT a carry/cost or
+   net-alpha monitor, and it issues NO decay verdict: #55's thresholds were stamped on a different α/band book (its own
+   CALIB_IDENTITY line says so), and #55 pages its own ALERT/DECIDE/INCOMPLETE. Re-paging those here would be a second stream with a
+   different body that hash de-duplication cannot join (§5-5) — so this file pages ONLY when the source is missing, stale, unreadable,
+   unstamped, or contradicts itself.
+
+★ STATES (one per evaluation; `ok` is True only for the first two):
+    JUDGED                  a judged row (OK / ALERT / DECIDE), fresh, whose observed newest anchor keeps up with the expected frontier
+    NOT_JUDGED              level INCOMPLETE with its census and incomplete windows — the freshness gate WORKING; not_judged_reason
+                            names the missing anchors
+    LEDGER_ABSENT_IN_GRACE  no ledger yet, and the check runs before GRACE_UNTIL — a fixed instant (W1 live + 30 h), never reset by a
